WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.334
-Thank you, again, for coming on
the show. I appreciate it.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:07.033
But last time you were here, we
were talking about the Met Gala.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.367
-Yeah, that's right.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.767
-We were going to go to
the Met Gala in a few days.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.367
You get all dressed up.
You go to this beautiful event.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.367
-My God, crazy.
-Did you have fun?

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:14.801
What'd you think?
-I mean, I -- okay,

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.334
first of all, Jimmy, you were
one of like the two people

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:18.901
that I knew at the whole thing.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.567
So I just felt like
such a wallflower.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.234
But I saw you. And you remember
this. I saw you.

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:24.667
It was like
everybody was around.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:26.567
Justin Beiber had
just gotten on stage.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.634
And, you know,
you gave me a big hug.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.000
And you were like,
"I'm so happy you're here."

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.567
It was really nice.
It was a really nice moment.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.067
And then, afterwards,
when I was on the steps,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.234
I saw you on the bottom, and I
saw you flipping the barrier.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:40.400
You flipped over the barrier.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.801
'Cause there were all these fans
on the other side of the street.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.067
And they had been waiting
all night.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.801
And you were like --
You're a man of the people.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.934
You went over to say hi to them.
-That's right.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.167
Yeah, they were chanting.
They were, like,

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.567
daring me, almost,
to jump the barrier.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.968
-Absolutely. And you did.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.534
-I felt like
they were like, "Jimmy!"

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.534
And I go, "Dude, you want to
watch my climb this fence?

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:00.767
I'll do it."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.367
But it was like a fake bush
or something.

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.767
-It was.
It was like a fake bush.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:06.234
And I saw you -- I saw you going
like -- I saw you testing it

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.567
to make sure that it would
take your weight.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.667
And I kind of saw you, like,
maneuver yourself over.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:11.133
So I was like, "You know, I'm
going to do the same thing."

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:13.167
-Maneuver myself?
I jumped over the bush.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:14.434
[ Laughter ]
Jumped over.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:16.067
-Did you?
-Yeah.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.434
-Do we have a picture?

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.834
-Apparently, yeah,
I have a picture.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.300
Oh, this is you.
-That's me.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.334
-Wait, you jumped the bush?

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.067
-Yeah, 'cause I jumped in
after you.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.367
'Cause I was like,
"If Jimmy Fallon is going to go

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:28.434
and say hi to the fans who have
been waiting all night,

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.267
for a glimpse of the stars, then
I want to do the same thing."

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.501
I wanted go and spend some time
with them.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.467
-You're a good man.
Look, here's Simu Liu.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.901
Look at this.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:40.133
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.334
Clearing the bush. And then you
go right into the street.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.133
-Mostly it's a shot of
my ass, but yeah.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.467
-No, I love that. Alright,
so here's a picture of me.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.934
Oh, I see what you're saying.

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.434
Well, it was --

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:54.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:56.767
I mean, they're similar --
they're similar photos.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.400
I mean, I don't know.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.267
I was just trying to get over --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.133
-I mean, I can't tell.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.133
-Our athletic ability
is kind of equal.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:07.567
People kind of confuse --
-You could be my stunt double.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:09.534
I tell them that all the time.
-Yeah. Thank you so much.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.734
Appreciate it. I mean, hey,
probably going to be a sequel.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.634
Just saying.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:18.534
By the way, I did a little
research, as I do all my guests.

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.501
But I realized we have
something in common

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.834
that I did not know about.
-Yes.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.801
-We both worked at
Abercrombie &amp; Fitch.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.534
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.133
That is correct.

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.901
-No, I think they're laughing

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.634
because they don't believe
that I would work.

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.534
Yeah, I worked at
Abercrombie &amp; Fitch.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:36.801
-That's amazing.
When were you there?

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:39.934
-Back when video games were --

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.367
I was in college, so I'd say
'94, '95, something like that.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.934
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah. When were you there?

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.234
-I would have been 6 years old
then, so maybe not then.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:53.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:57.033
It was a college job for me.
-Me too.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.434
-Yeah, I just remember --

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:00.767
I mean, it was such a status
symbol, right, to be like --

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:03.200
Well, first of all, like I knew
people who got scouted.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.334
Like, you know the routine.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:08.133
Like, you got scouted, like, you
know, going through the store.

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.968
Somebody would come up to you
and be like "Hi, excuse me.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:12.133
Have you ever thought of working
for Abercrombie &amp; Fitch?"

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:17.167
And if you had the look,
you would be offered a job.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.934
And so I, being like 17 years
old and super insecure,

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.834
like, I wanted very badly
to be hot.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.100
And I didn't realize it was
something that I can't control.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.033
So I would, like, go through
the store on my own.

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.634
And I would just be like
pretending to go through

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.901
clothes and being like...

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:37.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.701
Like, you know, "Excuse me, do
you need help with anything?"

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:45.000
And I'd be like "Oh, me?
No, no, I'm [Chuckles] okay."

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:50.033
And I never got asked, you know,
one single time.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:53.868
So this went on for a bit longer
than I'd like to admit.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:56.033
And then one day, I was finally
like, "You know what?

00:03:56.033 --> 00:04:00.100
Simu, you just got to take your
destiny into your own hands."

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.634
I walked into that Abercrombie
&amp; Fitch with a résumé.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.334
And I remember asking
for the manager.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.834
The manager's name was Brandon.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.000
He was wearing --

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.534
-That's one of the parts of
getting hired.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:11.067
You had to be named Brandon.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.968
-You got to go through Brandon.

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:15.501
He had, like, ripped jeans.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.567
-He was training to be
a firefighter, you know.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:22.234
And he looks me up and down
and he was like, "Eh, okay."

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:25.267
And he invited me to do a group
interview, which I slayed.

00:04:25.267 --> 00:04:26.701
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.467
And you became an employee.
-And I became an employee.

00:04:29.467 --> 00:04:31.801
Although, they call them --
they don't call them employees.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:35.334
They call them models.
I was a "model."

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.801
-I think they changed the name
after I worked there.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.067
I worked there
before they opened.

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.701
'Cause I -- and I went
in there --

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.868
[ Laughter ]
They weren't open.

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:48.601
They weren't open.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.000
I was putting shelves
on the wall and stuff.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.100
[ Laughter ]
-Okay. Oh, got it.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.467
-That's probably why
they hired me.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.100
-Doing construction
for Abercrombie.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.400
-Yeah, "You can work in
the backroom or something.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.701
Just don't be in front
of the house."

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.968
But I would go shirtless
and just...

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.634
[ Laughter ]
...stock the shelves.

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.000
-Did they want you
to go shirtless?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.334
-No, no, no. I got in
a lot of trouble for that.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:08.100
[ Laughter ]
But I went with my roommate,

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.767
because if you did get
a job there,

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:12.634
they would give you a free shirt
and a free pair of pants.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:13.667
-Oh, yeah. Nice, nice.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:14.834
-It's not free, but they give it

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:15.934
so you can wear that
as a uniform.

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:18.400
So he got a different shirt
and pants,

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.934
and then we would like swap.
-Swap.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:22.634
We were like "The Sisterhood of
the Traveling Pants."

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:23.834
-Nice. Nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.701
-And so that was
our college wardrobe.

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:27.467
And then, once it opened,
we quit.

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:28.734
-Fair enough.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.334
-Couldn't take it, man.
I was like, "No."

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.300
How long did you last there?

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.667
-You know, it's really
the status of it was so --

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:38.133
like, I loved being able to tell
my friends that I worked at

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:39.767
Abercrombie &amp; Fitch so much.

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.300
It took a long time.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.634
-Is this when you were in
the dance troupe?

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.033
-Yeah, around the same time.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.767
-We almost talked about it
last time,

00:05:47.767 --> 00:05:49.868
because I loved the name
of your team.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.701
-Yeah.
-What was it? Like cowboys --

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:54.067
-No, it was Hip-Hop Western.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:56.234
-Hip-Hop Western.
-Hip-Hop Western was --

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:58.133
-Western, yeah, 'cause Western
was the name

00:05:58.133 --> 00:05:59.300
of the university
that I went to --

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.501
University of Western Ontario.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:02.901
[ Cheers ]
Yes!

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.367
-No one's ever heard of that
in their lifetime.

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:07.434
[ Laughter ]
Western Ontario.

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:09.767
So wait.
And so you were Hip-Hop Western.

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.434
-Hip-Hop Western. That's right.

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.167
We came fourth place

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:16.934
at the provincial college
hip-hop competition.

00:06:16.934 --> 00:06:19.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
So, um...

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.467
-That goes on your résumé
immediately?

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:23.467
-You know, immediately.
-Did you have a go-to move?

00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:25.100
Do you have a signature move?

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.901
-I don't think I was good enough
to have a signature --

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.400
Well, we have styles, right?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.100
And, like, if you were a member
of, like, the 2008/2009,

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.000
it was all like, "So you think
you can dance."

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.000
It was like pop and lock,
"America's Best Dance Crew."

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.234
So we were all doing that,

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.334
like the robot and the body
waves and stuff.

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:40.300
-You think you still got
a little in you?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.667
-Oh, man.
[ Drumroll ]

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:43.934
Well, okay, if he's gonna --
Okay.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.100
-We got a beat going?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.601
Roots, want to give him a beat?

00:06:46.601 --> 00:06:50.300
-I'm not sure if it's working.
♪♪

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:54.534
Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.534 --> 00:06:55.634
-Oh!

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:58.234
♪♪

00:06:58.234 --> 00:07:00.133
Yes!

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.767
More with Simu Liu
after the break! Stick around!

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:12.133
♪♪

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:21.467
♪♪

